  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Application Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving deep into the application\'s requirements now. \"Resume Generation Pipeline\" is the name, and the goal is AI-powered resume compilation, integrating Gemini and Google Workspace. I\'m focusing on the metadata.json update as a primary focus point and then will move on to the pipeline stages.\n\n\n**Defining System Functionality**\n\nI\'ve got a much clearer picture now. I\'m focusing on the pipeline stages and visual statuses. I\'m planning out Google Sheets integration, mapping columns, and handling job description processing. Gemini\'s AI generation rules are becoming increasingly well-defined, with strict anti-hallucination measures and output formatting. LaTeX generation, PDF compilation, and Drive integration are shaping up nicely, with error handling.\n\n\n\n**Refining Interface Specifications**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI specifications and key user interactions. The focus is on the credentials UI, the Google Workspace integration (OAuth), and Gemini\'s status visibility. I\'ve also just been refining the generated resume preview, including ATS keyword analysis, PDF preview options, and the Drive integration link. I\'m building out a demo mode with realistic candidate profiles and job descriptions, and I\'ve started the implementation for the retry mechanism to commit to Sheets.\n\n\n**Integrating Audio Transcription**\n\nI\'m now integrating audio transcription using `gemini-3.5-flash`, which is a high-value feature for job descriptions and notes. In demo mode, it\'ll simulate the calls; in live mode, it will connect to Gemini directly. The OAuth setup is triggered when users request Google Sheets/Drive integration, specifically calling `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false`.\n\n\n**Prioritizing OAuth Configuration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the Google Sheets integration and OAuth 2.0. The minimal required scopes are clear, and I\'m debating the best setup order. The key is that the OAuth configuration is MANDATORY per the `SKILL.md` instructions before any Workspace API code. So I must call `set_up_oauth` first, especially considering `userConfirmedInUI: false`. This means I must pause code generation until confirmation. This blocks all other progress.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 135210837
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
