  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Audio Transcription**\n\nI\'m now focused on incorporating audio transcription using the specified model. I\'ve begun to evaluate the technical implications of adding this functionality, ensuring it aligns with the user\'s instructions and the project\'s overall scope. Specifically, I\'m thinking through how to best integrate the Gemini model for this task.\n\n\n**Analyzing Pipeline Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details of the resume generation pipeline. I\'m focusing on the features and sections required, starting with the application name, header, and the pipeline progress indicator. I\'m making sure to consider the user interface elements like the run button, demo mode, and Google OAuth integration, too.\n\n\n**Defining User Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing the user interface elements. I\'m focusing on the primary views, especially the configuration settings. I\'m concentrating on the Google Workspace configuration, including OAuth status, spreadsheet input, worksheet selection, candidate row selection, and Google Drive folder settings with sharing mode options and security explanations. I also have the visual column mapping interface well in mind.\n\n\n**Refining Settings and Options**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the AI and generation settings. I\'m considering parameters like the Gemini model selector and temperature adjustments, along with retry counts and strict anti-hallucination controls. I\'m also refining the resume formatting rules, including page targets, bullet limits, and project inclusion, alongside typography choices and margin preferences. I\'m also focused on pipeline execution options like sequential versus batch, and log levels. I\'ve re-iterated the voice dictation features to enable audio-to-text.\n\n\n**Examining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now deeply involved in the interface, specifically focusing on the logging and worksheet row tracking features. I\'m prioritizing interactive elements like filtering logs by severity and providing action buttons for log management. The candidate table is taking shape with columns for status badges and actions like running or inspecting rows. I\'m also planning the \"Generated Resumes & Preview\" tab with an ATS match score and hallucination audit.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on incorporating interactive PDF previews and LaTeX source inspection, allowing users to download PDFs and view the underlying LaTeX code with syntax highlighting. I\'m also adding functionality for custom regeneration and retry options, enhancing user control over the resume generation. I\'m now integrating JD analysis, including real-time Gemini breakdowns of skills and ATS terminology, with audio input to complement it.\n\n\n**Integrating API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now integrating the backend API endpoints. I\'m focusing on the `/api/gemini/generate-resume` endpoint for JSON schema generation and the `/api/gemini/transcribe-audio` endpoint for audio transcription using the Gemini model. I\'m also working on the `/api/latex/compile` endpoint for PDF generation and the `/api/health` endpoint for server status.\n\nI\'m also setting up Vite middleware for development and static distribution for production.\nI have also begun work on client-side Google Workspace integration. It uses `firebase-applet-config.json` with Firebase Auth and GoogleAuthProvider, and uses direct Google Sheets and Drive API calls.\n\n\n**Structuring Code Elements**\n\nI\'m now focused on the code structure, designing with clean organization in mind. I\'m defining TypeScript types for the core data and I\'m separating client-side service calls for Gemini, LaTeX, PDF, Sheets, Drive, OAuth, and audio processing. I\'m also preparing sample data for comprehensive testing and demo mode. Finally, I\'m integrating Firebase Auth for Google OAuth and token management.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 305376449
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
