  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focused on building the UI components, starting with `/src/components/Header.tsx`. I\'ve added the application title \"Resume Generation Pipeline,\" a version badge for \"v1.0.0,\" and a subtitle outlining the core functionality. I\'m also planning to incorporate status indicators for Google Account and Gemini Backend.\n\n\n**Adding Pipeline Controls**\n\nI\'ve been working on the UI controls for running the pipeline and have the \"Run Pipeline\" button with options now. I\'ve also incorporated a connection test button and a Demo Mode switch for the UI. Next, I\'m focusing on a visual progress component. I\'m also now designing the animated visual status indicators for each pipeline stage.\n\n\n**Defining Pipeline Parameters**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the pipeline\'s behavior. I\'m setting target rules for resume generation, including single/dual-page options, bullet point and project limits, and control of social links. Additionally, I\'m defining the execution flow, including sequential vs. batch processing, the handling of errors, and the logging verbosity.\n\n\n**Designing Resume View**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the resume display area. I\'m planning a layout with the candidate profile summary on the left, target role and ATS match rate (e.g., 94%) in the center, and a PDF preview on the right. The PDF section will include a LaTeX source inspector, and download options. I am also working on `JDAnalyzer.tsx`, which will have JD input options, and a Gemini-powered breakdown. I am also designing a credential modal.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
