42\200\224 VERY IMPORTANT\n\nI need one **very obvious configuration variable** where I can control how many jobs are searched/fetched.\n\nFor example:\n\n```python\nJOBS_TO_FETCH = 140\n```\n\nIf tomorrow I want only 70 jobs, I should only need to change:\n\n```python\nJOBS_TO_FETCH = 70\n```\n\nI should NOT have to search through the rest of the code to find where the job count is controlled.\n\nPut this variable near the top of the configuration section and clearly comment it.\n\nIf different candidates need different job counts, optionally support:\n\n```python\nCANDIDATE_JOB_LIMITS = {\n    \"Person X\": 140,\n    \"Person Y\": 70,\n    \"Person Z\": 100\n}\n```\n\nBut keep the implementation simple if a global job count is sufficient.\n\n---\n\n# 4. INFORMATION TO COLLECT FOR EACH JOB\n\nFor every job found, collect at minimum:\n\n1. Company Name\n2. Job Title / Role\n3. Location\n4. Application Link\n5. Full Job Description\n\nThe Job Description is required because it will be used later for resume generation.\n\n---\n\n# 5. GOOGLE SHEET \342\200\224 ONE SHEET PER CANDIDATE\n\nEach candidate will have their own Google Sheet/account.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nCandidate A \342\206\222 Candidate A Google Sheet\nCandidate B \342\206\222 Candidate B Google Sheet\nCandidate C \342\206\222 Candidate C Google Sheet\n```\n\nDo not mix candidate data.\n\nFor every job, add one row to the appropriate candidate\'s Google Sheet.\n\nThe columns should be approximately:\n\n| Company Name | Role | Location | Application Link | Resume |\n| ------------ | ---- | -------- | ---------------- | ------ |\n\nThe Resume column will contain a clickable Google Drive link to the resume generated specifically for that job.\n\n---\n\n# 6. JOB ROW + RESUME CONNECTION\n\nThis is extremely important.\n\nEvery job must have exactly the corresponding resume linked to it.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nRow 1:\nGoogle | Software Engineer | California | Application Link | Person X 5EXP 1\n\nRow 2:\nMicrosoft | SDET | Washington | Application Link | Person X 5EXP 2\n\nRow 3:\nAmazon | Software Engineer | Texas | Application Link | Person X 5EXP 3\n```\n\nThe Resume column should contain a clickable link to the actual PDF stored in Google Drive.\n\nTherefore:\n\n```text\nJob 1 \342\206\222 Resume 1\nJob 2 \342\206\222 Resume 2\nJob 3 \342\206\222 Resume 3\n```\n\nNever attach the wrong candidate\'s resume or the wrong job\'s resume.\n\n---\n\n# 7. RESUME GENERATION\n\nAfter collecting the jobs, generate a **job-specific tailored resume for each job**.\n\nI will provide:\n\n1. Resume-generation rules\n2. Candidate-specific resume information\n3. Master resume\n4. Exact master LaTeX code/template\n5. Formatting requirements\n6. ATS requirements\n7. Sections that may be changed\n8. Sections that must remain unchanged\n\nThe resume-generation system must follow the rules I provide.\n\nDo NOT invent a different resume structure.\n\nDo NOT replace my master LaTeX template with another template.\n\nDo NOT change information that my rules say must remain unchanged.\n\nThe job description should be used to tailor the allowed resume sections appropriately.\n\n---\n\n# 8. RESUME GENERATION FLOW\n\nThe expected process is:\n\n```text\nCandidate Profile\n       +\nCandidate Resume Rules\n       +\nMaster LaTeX Resume\n       +\nJob Description\n       \342\206\223\nResume Generation AI\n       \342\206\223\nTailored LaTeX Code\n       \342\206\223\nLaTeX Compilation\n       \342\206\223\nFinal PDF Resume\n```\n\nThe final output should be a PDF.\n\n---\n\n# 9. GOOGLE DRIVE ORGANIZATION\n\nEach candidate must have a separate Google Drive folder.\n\nInside that candidate\'s folder, create a folder for the current date.\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nYYYY-MM-DD\n```\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\n2026-08-23\n```\n\nStructure:\n\n```text\nCandidate A\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 2026-08-23\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Person X 5EXP 1.pdf\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Person X 5EXP 2.pdf\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Person X 5EXP 3.pdf\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ...\n```\n\nFor Candidate B:\n\n```text\nCandidate B\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 2026-08-23\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Person Y 5EXP 1.pdf\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Person Y 5EXP 2.pdf\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Person Y 5EXP 3.pdf\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ...\n```\n\nIf the date folder already exists, use it.\n\nIf it does not exist, create it automatically.\n\n---\n\n# 10. RESUME FILE NAMING \342\200\224 VERY IMPORTANT\n\nThe resume filename must follow this exact pattern:\n\n```text\n<Candidate Name> <Experience Label> <Count>.pdf\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nPerson X 5EXP 1.pdf\nPerson X 5EXP 2.pdf\nPerson X 5EXP 3.pdf\n```\n\nFor another candidate:\n\n```text\nPerson Y 5EXP 1.pdf\nPerson Y 5EXP 2.pdf\nPerson Y 5EXP 3.pdf\n```\n\nThe candidate\'s experience label should be configurable.\n\nFor example:\n\n```python\n\"experience_label\": \"5EXP\"\n```\n\nThen the filename can automatically be generated with:\n\n```python\nf\"{candidate[\'name\']} {candidate[\'experience_label\']} {resume_count}.pdf\"\n```\n\nDo not manually hardcode every filename.\n\n---\n\n# 11. RESUME COUNTING\n\nThe resume number must be **independent for each candidate**.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nCandidate A:\nPerson X 5EXP 1.pdf\nPerson X 5EXP 2.pdf\nPerson X 5EXP 3.pdf\n\nCandidate B:\nPerson Y 5EXP 1.pdf\nPerson Y 5EXP 2.pdf\nPerson Y 5EXP 3.pdf\n```\n\nCandidate B must start from 1 for their own resumes.\n\nCandidate A\'s count must never affect Candidate B\'s count.\n\nThe system should automatically increment the number as each resume is successfully generated.\n\nIdeally, the system should determine the next available count in the candidate\'s date folder to avoid overwriting an existing file.\n\n---\n\n# 12. GOOGLE SHEET RESUME LINK\n\nAfter generating the PDF:\n\n1. Save the PDF to the correct candidate\'s Google Drive.\n2. Get the Google Drive URL.\n3. Put that URL in the Resume column of the exact corresponding job row.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nJob:\nGoogle \342\200\223 Software Engineer\n\nResume:\nPerson X 5EXP 1.pdf\n\nGoogle Sheet:\nResume column \342\206\222 clickable Google Drive link\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. COMPLETE END-TO-END FLOW\n\nThe entire system should work approximately like this:\n\n```text\nSTART\n  \342\206\223\nLoad candidate configurations\n  \342\206\223\nFor each candidate\n  \342\206\223\nRead candidate profile\n  \342\206\223\nRead target roles and keywords\n  \342\206\223\nSearch jobs\n  \342\206\223\nFetch configured number of jobs\n  \342\206\223\nExtract:\n    Company\n    Role\n    Location\n    Application Link\n    Job Description\n  \342\206\223\nCheck for duplicate jobs\n  \342\206\223\nSave jobs to candidate\'s Google Sheet\n  \342\206\223\nFor each job\n  \342\206\223\nRead candidate\'s resume rules\n  \342\206\223\nRead candidate\'s master LaTeX\n  \342\206\223\nSend Job Description + Resume Rules + Master LaTeX\nto Resume Generation AI\n  \342\206\223\nGenerate tailored LaTeX\n  \342\206\223\nCompile LaTeX \342\206\222 PDF\n  \342\206\223\nGenerate next resume number\n  \342\206\223\nCreate/find candidate\'s date folder\n  \342\206\223\nSave PDF using:\n<Candidate Name> <Experience> <Count>.pdf\n  \342\206\223\nGet Google Drive URL\n  \342\206\223\nUpdate corresponding Google Sheet row\n  \342\206\223\nPut resume link in Resume column\n  \342\206\223\nMove to next job\n  \342\206\223\nMove to next candidate\n  \342\206\223\nEND\n```\n\n---\n\n# 14. DUPLICATE JOB HANDLING\n\nThe system should try to prevent duplicate jobs.\n\nUse a combination of:\n\n* Application URL\n* Company Name\n* Job Title\n\nto identify duplicates.\n\nIf the job already exists in that candidate\'s Google Sheet, do not add it again unless explicitly configured otherwise.\n\n---\n\n# 15. ERROR HANDLING\n\nA failure for one job should NOT stop the entire process.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nJob 1 \342\206\222 Success\nJob 2 \342\206\222 Success\nJob 3 \342\206\222 Resume generation failed\nJob 4 \342\206\222 Success\n```\n\nThe system should log Job 3 as failed and continue with Job 4.\n\nHandle errors such as:\n\n* Job search failure\n* Missing job description\n* Missing application link\n* Resume generation failure\n* Invalid LaTeX\n* LaTeX compilation failure\n* Google Drive upload failure\n* Google Sheet update failure\n* Duplicate job\n* Duplicate filename\n\n---\n\n# 16. LOGGING\n\nProvide clear logs during execution.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n[Candidate] Person X\n[Job Search] Fetching 140 jobs\n\n[Job 1] Google - Software Engineer\n[Resume] Generating tailored resume\n[LaTeX] Compilation successful\n[Drive] Saved: Person X 5EXP 1.pdf\n[Sheet] Resume link added\n[Job 1] Completed\n\n[Job 2] Microsoft - SDET\n[Resume] Generating tailored resume\n[LaTeX] Compilation successful\n[Drive] Saved: Person X 5EXP 2.pdf\n[Sheet] Resume link added\n[Job 2] Completed\n```\n\nAt the end, show a summary:\n\n```text\nCandidate: Person X\nJobs found: 140\nResumes generated: 138\nFailed: 2\n```\n\nThen continue with the next candidate.\n\n---\n\n# 17. CONFIGURATION STRUCTURE\n\nKeep all important configuration in one easy-to-find section.\n\nFor example:\n\n```python\n# ==========================================\n# MAIN CONFIGURATION\n# ==========================================\n\nJOBS_TO_FETCH = 140\n\nCANDIDATES = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"Person X\",\n        \"email\": \"candidateA@example.com\",\n        \"experience_label\": \"5EXP\",\n\n        \"target_roles\": [\n            \"Software Developer\",\n            \"SDET\"\n        ],\n\n        \"keywords\": [\n            \"Python\",\n            \"Java\",\n            \"Selenium\"\n        ],\n\n        \"google_sheet\": \"SHEET_A\",\n        \"google_drive_folder\": \"DRIVE_FOLDER_A\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\nThe exact structure can be improved if necessary, but it must remain easy for me to modify.\n\n---\n\n# 18. MODULAR CODE\n\nDo not write separate duplicated code for every candidate.\n\nAvoid:\n\n```python\nsearch_candidate_a()\nsearch_candidate_b()\nsearch_candidate_c()\n```\n\nInstead, use reusable functions such as:\n\n```python\nprocess_candidate(candidate)\nsearch_jobs(candidate)\ngenerate_resume(candidate, job)\ncompile_latex(...)\nupload_resume(...)\nupdate_google_sheet(...)\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```python\nfor candidate in CANDIDATES:\n    process_candidate(candidate)\n```\n\nThis should allow me to add Candidate D simply by adding another configuration entry.\n\n---\n\n# 19. IMPORTANT CANDIDATE SEPARATION\n\nThe following must always remain candidate-specific:\n\n```text\nCandidate\n    \342\206\223\nJob Search\n    \342\206\223\nGoogle Sheet\n    \342\206\223\nResume Rules\n    \342\206\223\nMaster LaTeX\n    \342\206\223\nGoogle Drive Folder\n    \342\206\223\nDate Folder\n    \342\206\223\nResume Counter\n```\n\nCandidate A\'s information must never be used for Candidate B.\n\n---\n\n# 20. WHAT I WILL PROVIDE\n\nI will give you the following information after this prompt.\n\n## Candidate Details\n\nFor each candidate:\n\n```text\nCandidate Name:\nEmail:\nExperience:\nTarget Roles:\nSkills:\nLocation Preference:\nJob Search Keywords:\nGoogle Sheet:\nGoogle Drive Folder:\n```\n\n## Resume Details\n\nFor each candidate, I will provide:\n\n1. Resume-generation rules\n2. Master resume\n3. Master LaTeX code\n4. Formatting requirements\n5. ATS requirements\n6. Sections that can be modified\n7. Sections that cannot be modified\n8. Any candidate-specific restrictions\n\n## Existing Code\n\nI will also provide my existing job-search/resume automation code.\n\n---\n\n# 21. YOUR TASK\n\nAfter I provide the candidate details, resume rules, master LaTeX code, and existing code:\n\n### First, analyze the existing code.\n\nTell me:\n\n1. What functionality already exists.\n2. What can be reused.\n3. What needs to be modified.\n4. What needs to be added.\n5. Whether the current job-search architecture can support multiple candidates.\n6. How Google Sheets should be integrated.\n7. How Google Drive should be integrated.\n8. How the resume-generation pipeline should be integrated.\n9. How the resume counter should work.\n10. How each resume will be connected to the correct job row.\n\n### Then implement the required changes.\n\nDo not remove existing functionality unnecessarily.\n\nDo not rewrite the entire project from scratch if the existing code can be extended cleanly.\n\nDo not assume missing information.\n\nIf something is required but I have not provided it, clearly tell me what is missing.\n\n---\n\n# 22. FINAL REQUIREMENTS\n\nThe final system MUST:\n\n* Support multiple candidates.\n* Allow different job profiles for each candidate.\n* Allow different resume rules for each candidate.\n* Allow different master LaTeX templates for each candidate if necessary.\n* Allow an easily configurable job count.\n* Search jobs separately for every candidate.\n* Store Company Name, Role, Location, Application Link and Resume in Google Sheets.\n* Use a separate Google Sheet for each candidate.\n* Generate a tailored resume for every selected job.\n* Follow my master LaTeX template and resume rules.\n* Compile the LaTeX into PDF.\n* Save resumes directly to the correct candidate\'s Google Drive.\n* Create/use a date folder such as `2026-08-23`.\n* Name resumes exactly like:\n  `Person X 5EXP 1.pdf`\n  `Person X 5EXP 2.pdf`\n  `Person X 5EXP 3.pdf`\n* Maintain a separate resume counter for every candidate.\n* Never mix candidates.\n* Put the exact Google Drive resume link beside the corresponding job in the Google Sheet.\n* Handle failures without stopping the entire pipeline.\n* Provide useful execution logs.\n* Prevent duplicate jobs where possible.\n* Be easy to maintain and extend.\n\nI will now provide the **existing code, candidate details, resume rules, and master LaTeX code**. Review all of them together before proposing the final implementation."
    }
  }
}
