  planner_response {
    response: "Here is the structural and technical analysis of the existing codebase against your requirements for the multi-candidate job automation and resume generation pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### 1. What Functionality Already Exists\n\n* **Full-Stack Gemini AI Engine (`/server/gemini.ts` & `/src/services/geminiService.ts`)**: Structured extraction, job description semantic analysis, ATS keyword harvesting, and prompt engineering with anti-hallucination factual guardrails.\n* **LaTeX Generation & PDF Engine (`/src/services/latexService.ts` & `/src/services/pdfService.ts`)**: Dynamic LaTeX compilation with symbol escaping, ATS formatting, and PDF rendering.\n* **Google Workspace OAuth & API Integration (`/src/services/oauthService.ts`, `sheetsService.ts`, `driveService.ts`)**: Client-side OAuth 2.0 flow, Google Sheets reading/updating with cell hyperlinking (`=HYPERLINK(...)`), and Google Drive file uploads with permissions.\n* **Orchestration & State Management (`/src/services/pipelineService.ts`)**: Pipeline state machine with logging, progress tracking, cancellation support, and single-candidate vs. batch runner logic.\n* **Interactive UI (`/src/App.tsx`, `/src/components/*`)**: 7-stage visual pipeline monitor, candidate data tables, live telemetry logs, dual-pane PDF & LaTeX previewers, JD analyzer, and settings panels.\n\n---\n\n### 2. What Can Be Reused\n\n* **Google Drive Upload & URL Resolution (`driveService.ts`)**: Folder lookup/creation, direct PDF upload, and shareable web link generation.\n* **Google Sheets Row Update Logic (`sheetsService.ts`)**: Row-by-row updates and cell formula linking.\n* **Server-Side Gemini AI Endpoints (`/api/gemini/*`)**: Proxy routes keeping Gemini API credentials secured on the server.\n* **LaTeX Compilation Pipeline (`pdfService.ts`)**: Automated LaTeX to PDF rendering pipeline.\n* **Error Resilience Architecture**: Per-record `try/catch` boundaries ensuring failures in one item do not abort the entire pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### 3. What Needs to Be Modified\n\n* **Candidate Configuration Architecture**: Shift from a single spreadsheet configuration model to a candidate configuration array (`CANDIDATES = [...]`) where each candidate encapsulates their own target roles, experience label, keywords, resume rules, master LaTeX template, Google Sheet ID, and Google Drive folder.\n* **Global Job Limit Control**: Add a prominent `JOBS_TO_FETCH = 140` configuration at the very top of the configuration module (with optional candidate-specific overrides `CANDIDATE_JOB_LIMITS`).\n* **Resume Naming Standard**: Replace generic naming with the strict standard:\n  ```text\n  <Candidate Name> <Experience Label> <Count>.pdf\n  # e.g., Person X 5EXP 1.pdf\n  ```\n* **Drive Folder Structure**: Enforce candidate-specific root folders containing auto-created daily subfolders formatted as `YYYY-MM-DD` (e.g., `2026-08-23`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. What Needs to Be Added\n\n* **Multi-Candidate Job Search Engine (`/src/services/jobSearchService.ts`)**: A dedicated search module that queries jobs specifically for each candidate\'s target roles, experience level, keywords, and location preferences without data crossover.\n* **Job Deduplication Engine**: An automatic filter checking `(Application URL, Company Name, Job Title)` against candidate history and existing Google Sheet rows before processing.\n* **Candidate-Specific Resume Counters**: Independent counters tracking generated resumes per candidate within their daily date folder.\n* **Candidate Master Profile & LaTeX Rule Injector**: Support for candidate-specific master LaTeX templates, ATS rules, and locked vs. modifiable section boundaries.\n* **Candidate Switcher & Multi-Candidate Batch Dashboard UI**: UI controls allowing selection and execution for individual candidates or automated sequential execution across all configured candidates.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Whether the Current Job-Search Architecture Can Support Multiple Candidates\n\n* **Current Status**: The existing code focused on processing pre-loaded candidate rows rather than autonomous multi-candidate job searching.\n* **Upgrade Strategy**: We will implement a modular `searchJobsForCandidate(candidate, limit)` module. It iterates sequentially over `CANDIDATES`, fetching candidate-specific jobs up to `JOBS_TO_FETCH`, ensuring Candidate A\'s queries and results are completely isolated from Candidate B\'s.\n\n---\n\n### 6. How Google Sheets Should Be Integrated\n\n* **One Sheet per Candidate**: Each candidate configuration specifies their own `google_sheet` spreadsheet ID.\n* **Target Schema**:\n  | Company Name | Role | Location | Application Link | Resume |\n  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n* **Deduplication Check**: When reading the candidate\'s sheet at the start of a run, the system scans existing application links/titles to prevent inserting duplicates.\n* **Drive Hyperlink**: Upon PDF generation and Drive upload, the `Resume` column is written with an active link to the PDF in Google Drive.\n\n---\n\n### 7. How Google Drive Should Be Integrated\n\n* **Candidate Root Folder**: Resolved using `candidate.google_drive_folder`.\n* **Daily Subfolder Creation**: On execution, the system checks for or creates a folder matching the current date (`YYYY-MM-DD`, e.g., `2026-08-23`).\n* **Upload**: The compiled PDF is uploaded directly to that date folder and assigned appropriate viewing permissions.\n\n---\n\n### 8. How the Resume-Generation Pipeline Should Be Integrated\n\n* **Data Synthesis**:\n  $$\\text{Candidate Profile} + \\text{Resume Rules} + \\text{Master LaTeX} + \\text{Job Description} \\xrightarrow{\\text{Gemini AI}} \\text{Tailored LaTeX}$$\n* **Rule Enforcement**: The prompt strictly protects immutable sections (contact info, core institutions, verified credentials) while tailoring relevant experience bullet points and technical skill groupings to match the job description.\n* **Compilation**: The generated LaTeX is compiled to PDF and passed directly to the Drive uploader.\n\n---\n\n### 9. How the Resume Counter Should Work\n\n* **Independent Per Candidate**:\n  * Candidate A counter: `Person X 5EXP 1.pdf`, `Person X 5EXP 2.pdf`, `Person X 5EXP 3.pdf`\n  * Candidate B counter: `Person Y 5EXP 1.pdf`, `Person Y 5EXP 2.pdf`\n* **Inspection**: The system queries the candidate\'s date folder on Google Drive to discover existing files, finding the highest existing count $N$ and automatically starting the next resume at $N+1$.\n\n---\n\n### 10. How Each Resume Will Be Connected to the Correct Job Row\n\n* **Synchronous Sequential Processing**:\n  1. Job row $i$ is identified or inserted into Candidate $K$\'s Google Sheet.\n  2. Resume $i$ is generated for Job $i$ using Candidate $K$\'s master LaTeX.\n  3. Resume $i$ is compiled to PDF with filename `CandidateK ExperienceLabel i.pdf`.\n  4. PDF is uploaded to Candidate $K$\'s `YYYY-MM-DD` Drive folder.\n  5. The resulting Drive link is written to column 5 (\"Resume\") of row $i$ in Candidate $K$\'s Sheet.\n\n---\n\n### Ready for Your Candidate & Template Data\n\nPlease provide:\n1. **Candidate Details** (Name, email, experience label, target roles, skills, search keywords, Google Sheet IDs, Google Drive folder IDs).\n2. **Resume Details** (Master resume text, master LaTeX templates, allowed/locked sections, ATS rules).\n3. **Existing Job-Search Code or Preferences**.\n\nOnce provided, I will implement the modular multi-candidate pipeline."
    modified_response: "Here is the structural and technical analysis of the existing codebase against your requirements for the multi-candidate job automation and resume generation pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### 1. What Functionality Already Exists\n\n* **Full-Stack Gemini AI Engine (`/server/gemini.ts` & `/src/services/geminiService.ts`)**: Structured extraction, job description semantic analysis, ATS keyword harvesting, and prompt engineering with anti-hallucination factual guardrails.\n* **LaTeX Generation & PDF Engine (`/src/services/latexService.ts` & `/src/services/pdfService.ts`)**: Dynamic LaTeX compilation with symbol escaping, ATS formatting, and PDF rendering.\n* **Google Workspace OAuth & API Integration (`/src/services/oauthService.ts`, `sheetsService.ts`, `driveService.ts`)**: Client-side OAuth 2.0 flow, Google Sheets reading/updating with cell hyperlinking (`=HYPERLINK(...)`), and Google Drive file uploads with permissions.\n* **Orchestration & State Management (`/src/services/pipelineService.ts`)**: Pipeline state machine with logging, progress tracking, cancellation support, and single-candidate vs. batch runner logic.\n* **Interactive UI (`/src/App.tsx`, `/src/components/*`)**: 7-stage visual pipeline monitor, candidate data tables, live telemetry logs, dual-pane PDF & LaTeX previewers, JD analyzer, and settings panels.\n\n---\n\n### 2. What Can Be Reused\n\n* **Google Drive Upload & URL Resolution (`driveService.ts`)**: Folder lookup/creation, direct PDF upload, and shareable web link generation.\n* **Google Sheets Row Update Logic (`sheetsService.ts`)**: Row-by-row updates and cell formula linking.\n* **Server-Side Gemini AI Endpoints (`/api/gemini/*`)**: Proxy routes keeping Gemini API credentials secured on the server.\n* **LaTeX Compilation Pipeline (`pdfService.ts`)**: Automated LaTeX to PDF rendering pipeline.\n* **Error Resilience Architecture**: Per-record `try/catch` boundaries ensuring failures in one item do not abort the entire pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### 3. What Needs to Be Modified\n\n* **Candidate Configuration Architecture**: Shift from a single spreadsheet configuration model to a candidate configuration array (`CANDIDATES = [...]`) where each candidate encapsulates their own target roles, experience label, keywords, resume rules, master LaTeX template, Google Sheet ID, and Google Drive folder.\n* **Global Job Limit Control**: Add a prominent `JOBS_TO_FETCH = 140` configuration at the very top of the configuration module (with optional candidate-specific overrides `CANDIDATE_JOB_LIMITS`).\n* **Resume Naming Standard**: Replace generic naming with the strict standard:\n  ```text\n  <Candidate Name> <Experience Label> <Count>.pdf\n  # e.g., Person X 5EXP 1.pdf\n  ```\n* **Drive Folder Structure**: Enforce candidate-specific root folders containing auto-created daily subfolders formatted as `YYYY-MM-DD` (e.g., `2026-08-23`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. What Needs to Be Added\n\n* **Multi-Candidate Job Search Engine (`/src/services/jobSearchService.ts`)**: A dedicated search module that queries jobs specifically for each candidate\'s target roles, experience level, keywords, and location preferences without data crossover.\n* **Job Deduplication Engine**: An automatic filter checking `(Application URL, Company Name, Job Title)` against candidate history and existing Google Sheet rows before processing.\n* **Candidate-Specific Resume Counters**: Independent counters tracking generated resumes per candidate within their daily date folder.\n* **Candidate Master Profile & LaTeX Rule Injector**: Support for candidate-specific master LaTeX templates, ATS rules, and locked vs. modifiable section boundaries.\n* **Candidate Switcher & Multi-Candidate Batch Dashboard UI**: UI controls allowing selection and execution for individual candidates or automated sequential execution across all configured candidates.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Whether the Current Job-Search Architecture Can Support Multiple Candidates\n\n* **Current Status**: The existing code focused on processing pre-loaded candidate rows rather than autonomous multi-candidate job searching.\n* **Upgrade Strategy**: We will implement a modular `searchJobsForCandidate(candidate, limit)` module. It iterates sequentially over `CANDIDATES`, fetching candidate-specific jobs up to `JOBS_TO_FETCH`, ensuring Candidate A\'s queries and results are completely isolated from Candidate B\'s.\n\n---\n\n### 6. How Google Sheets Should Be Integrated\n\n* **One Sheet per Candidate**: Each candidate configuration specifies their own `google_sheet` spreadsheet ID.\n* **Target Schema**:\n  | Company Name | Role | Location | Application Link | Resume |\n  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n* **Deduplication Check**: When reading the candidate\'s sheet at the start of a run, the system scans existing application links/titles to prevent inserting duplicates.\n* **Drive Hyperlink**: Upon PDF generation and Drive upload, the `Resume` column is written with an active link to the PDF in Google Drive.\n\n---\n\n### 7. How Google Drive Should Be Integrated\n\n* **Candidate Root Folder**: Resolved using `candidate.google_drive_folder`.\n* **Daily Subfolder Creation**: On execution, the system checks for or creates a folder matching the current date (`YYYY-MM-DD`, e.g., `2026-08-23`).\n* **Upload**: The compiled PDF is uploaded directly to that date folder and assigned appropriate viewing permissions.\n\n---\n\n### 8. How the Resume-Generation Pipeline Should Be Integrated\n\n* **Data Synthesis**:\n  $$\\text{Candidate Profile} + \\text{Resume Rules} + \\text{Master LaTeX} + \\text{Job Description} \\xrightarrow{\\text{Gemini AI}} \\text{Tailored LaTeX}$$\n* **Rule Enforcement**: The prompt strictly protects immutable sections (contact info, core institutions, verified credentials) while tailoring relevant experience bullet points and technical skill groupings to match the job description.\n* **Compilation**: The generated LaTeX is compiled to PDF and passed directly to the Drive uploader.\n\n---\n\n### 9. How the Resume Counter Should Work\n\n* **Independent Per Candidate**:\n  * Candidate A counter: `Person X 5EXP 1.pdf`, `Person X 5EXP 2.pdf`, `Person X 5EXP 3.pdf`\n  * Candidate B counter: `Person Y 5EXP 1.pdf`, `Person Y 5EXP 2.pdf`\n* **Inspection**: The system queries the candidate\'s date folder on Google Drive to discover existing files, finding the highest existing count $N$ and automatically starting the next resume at $N+1$.\n\n---\n\n### 10. How Each Resume Will Be Connected to the Correct Job Row\n\n* **Synchronous Sequential Processing**:\n  1. Job row $i$ is identified or inserted into Candidate $K$\'s Google Sheet.\n  2. Resume $i$ is generated for Job $i$ using Candidate $K$\'s master LaTeX.\n  3. Resume $i$ is compiled to PDF with filename `CandidateK ExperienceLabel i.pdf`.\n  4. PDF is uploaded to Candidate $K$\'s `YYYY-MM-DD` Drive folder.\n  5. The resulting Drive link is written to column 5 (\"Resume\") of row $i$ in Candidate $K$\'s Sheet.\n\n---\n\n### Ready for Your Candidate & Template Data\n\nPlease provide:\n1. **Candidate Details** (Name, email, experience label, target roles, skills, search keywords, Google Sheet IDs, Google Drive folder IDs).\n2. **Resume Details** (Master resume text, master LaTeX templates, allowed/locked sections, ATS rules).\n3. **Existing Job-Search Code or Preferences**.\n\nOnce provided, I will implement the modular multi-candidate pipeline."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
