  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Job Search Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the core functionality for a job search service, specifically in `/src/services/jobSearchService.ts`. The initial plan is to build a function, `searchJobsForCandidate`, that takes a candidate profile and a search limit. I\'m prioritizing the mechanics of how it will return relevant job postings.\n\n\n**Refining Job Search**\n\nI\'ve been working to refine the job search functionality. Now, for each job, I\'m collecting the company name, job title, location, application link, and full description. I\'m also implementing deduplication, comparing against existing job postings, and adding tags for candidate ID, name, and status. I\'ve started thinking through helpers for file names, date folders, and matching allowed job titles. I\'m on track to build the service in `/src/services/jobSearchService.ts`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 948154383
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
