    response: "I have implemented the **Multi-Candidate Resume Automation Pipeline** adhering strictly to your candidate configurations, master LaTeX templates, and resume generation rules:\n\n- **Scalable Candidate Configuration**: Configured candidate profiles (**Lohith S**, **Smit Patel**, and **Vamsi Krishna**) with isolated target roles, keywords, experience histories, education records, Google Sheets, Google Drive folders, and master LaTeX templates in `src/data/candidateProfiles.ts`.\n- **Configurable Global Job Limits**: Embedded `JOBS_TO_FETCH = 140` prominently at the top of the configuration and in the interface with dynamic counter controls.\n- **Candidate Data Isolation & Deduplication**: Built a dedicated search and queue engine ensuring each candidate\'s jobs, Google Sheets, Drive folders, and resume counters remain isolated without cross-contamination.\n- **Enforced Strict Resume Generation Rules**:\n  1. **Professional Summary**: Single paragraph of 5\342\200\2236 lines (60\342\200\223100 words), starting with the matched Job Title from the allowed list + `with 5+ years of experience...`.\n  2. **Technical Skills**: Aligned to JD technologies.\n  3. **Professional Experience**: Exactly 4 concise bullet points under each locked company role with candidate-specific dates and locations.\n  4. **Technical Projects**: Exactly 2 dynamically generated projects tailored to the JD with 2 bullet points each.\n  5. **Education**: Preserved exactly with degree and institution (no dates).\n  6. **Header & Contact**: Cleaned to only include Name, Email, Phone, and `Open to Relocate`.\n  7. **Job Title Restrictions**: Mapped strictly to each candidate\'s allowed role list.\n  8. **LaTeX Escaping & Alignment**: Escapes special characters (`&`, `%`, `_`, `$`, `#`, `{`, `}`) and preserves exact document geometry, macros, and formatting.\n- **Automated Google Drive & Sheets Integration**: Automatically generates date subfolders (`YYYY-MM-DD`), formats standard filenames (`<Candidate Name> <Experience Label> <Count>.pdf`), and writes clickable Google Drive resume links to the Google Sheet rows.\n\nWhenever you are ready, please share the Job Description or any further instructions!"
    modified_response: "I have implemented the **Multi-Candidate Resume Automation Pipeline** adhering strictly to your candidate configurations, master LaTeX templates, and resume generation rules:\n\n- **Scalable Candidate Configuration**: Configured candidate profiles (**Lohith S**, **Smit Patel**, and **Vamsi Krishna**) with isolated target roles, keywords, experience histories, education records, Google Sheets, Google Drive folders, and master LaTeX templates in `src/data/candidateProfiles.ts`.\n- **Configurable Global Job Limits**: Embedded `JOBS_TO_FETCH = 140` prominently at the top of the configuration and in the interface with dynamic counter controls.\n- **Candidate Data Isolation & Deduplication**: Built a dedicated search and queue engine ensuring each candidate\'s jobs, Google Sheets, Drive folders, and resume counters remain isolated without cross-contamination.\n- **Enforced Strict Resume Generation Rules**:\n  1. **Professional Summary**: Single paragraph of 5\342\200\2236 lines (60\342\200\223100 words), starting with the matched Job Title from the allowed list + `with 5+ years of experience...`.\n  2. **Technical Skills**: Aligned to JD technologies.\n  3. **Professional Experience**: Exactly 4 concise bullet points under each locked company role with candidate-specific dates and locations.\n  4. **Technical Projects**: Exactly 2 dynamically generated projects tailored to the JD with 2 bullet points each.\n  5. **Education**: Preserved exactly with degree and institution (no dates).\n  6. **Header & Contact**: Cleaned to only include Name, Email, Phone, and `Open to Relocate`.\n  7. **Job Title Restrictions**: Mapped strictly to each candidate\'s allowed role list.\n  8. **LaTeX Escaping & Alignment**: Escapes special characters (`&`, `%`, `_`, `$`, `#`, `{`, `}`) and preserves exact document geometry, macros, and formatting.\n- **Automated Google Drive & Sheets Integration**: Automatically generates date subfolders (`YYYY-MM-DD`), formats standard filenames (`<Candidate Name> <Experience Label> <Count>.pdf`), and writes clickable Google Drive resume links to the Google Sheet rows.\n\nWhenever you are ready, please share the Job Description or any further instructions!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
