  planner_response {
    response: "Here are the exact answers to your two questions:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Where to See & Update the Workday and Easy Apply Counts\n\nIn your codebase and app interface, the counts are defined using the formula:\n$$\\text{Total Count} = \\text{Workday} + \\text{Easy Apply}$$\n\n#### A. In the Code (`src/data/candidateProfiles.ts`)\nYou can view and update the counts at the very top of `src/data/candidateProfiles.ts`:\n\n```typescript\n// ============================================================================\n// MAIN CONFIGURATION: WORKDAY, EASY APPLY & GLOBAL JOB FETCH LIMITS\n// ============================================================================\nexport const DEFAULT_MAX_WORKDAY_JOBS = 10;\nexport const DEFAULT_MAX_EASY_ATS_JOBS = 65;\nexport const JOBS_TO_FETCH = DEFAULT_MAX_WORKDAY_JOBS + DEFAULT_MAX_EASY_ATS_JOBS; // 75\n\n// Candidate Quotas:\n// 1. Lohith S:     Workday = 10, Easy Apply = 65, Total Count = 75\n// 2. Smit Patel:   Workday = 10, Easy Apply = 65, Total Count = 75\n// 3. Vamsi Krishna: Workday = 10, Easy Apply = 65, Total Count = 75\nexport const CANDIDATE_JOB_LIMITS = {\n  \'Lohith S\':     { workday: 10, easyAts: 65, total: 75 },\n  \'Smit Patel\':   { workday: 10, easyAts: 65, total: 75 },\n  \'Vamsi Krishna\': { workday: 10, easyAts: 65, total: 75 },\n};\n```\n\nAnd in each candidate object within the `CANDIDATES` array:\n* **LOHITH S**: `maxWorkdayJobs: 10`, `maxEasyAtsJobs: 65`, `maxTotalJobs: 75`\n* **Smit Patel**: `maxWorkdayJobs: 10`, `maxEasyAtsJobs: 65`, `maxTotalJobs: 75`\n* **Vamsi Krishna**: `maxWorkdayJobs: 10`, `maxEasyAtsJobs: 65`, `maxTotalJobs: 75`\n\n#### B. In the Live App Interface\n* Navigate to the **Multi-Candidate Automation** tab.\n* On each candidate card, you will see a dedicated quota breakdown box:\n  * **Total Count:** `75 jobs` (or your custom `JOBS_TO_FETCH`)\n  * **\342\200\242 Workday:** `10`\n  * **\342\200\242 Easy Apply:** `65`\n* The jobs table displays a **Platform (ATS)** column tagging each collected position with an amber `WORKDAY` or emerald `EASY_ATS` badge.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Run the Python Script (CLI Commands)\n\nYour Python script uses `argparse` with specific command-line flags. Here is how you run it:\n\n#### Basic Execution (Candidate Name Required)\nTo run for a specific candidate using their default config in `profiles.json`:\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\"\n```\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\"\n```\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\n#### Custom Quotas (Override Workday and Easy Apply from Command Line)\nIf you want to override the numbers dynamically when launching:\n```bash\n# Example: 15 Workday jobs + 50 Easy Apply jobs (Total = 65)\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" --workday 15 --easy 50\n```\n\n#### Scrape Only Mode (Without starting the resume customizer immediately)\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\" --scrape-only\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Available CLI Arguments:\n| Argument | Type | Default | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `--candidate` | `string` | **Required** | Candidate key in `profiles.json` (e.g. `\"Lohith S\"`, `\"Smit Patel\"`, `\"Vamsi Krishna\"`) |\n| `--workday` | `int` | `10` | Maximum number of Workday jobs to scrape |\n| `--easy` | `int` | `65` | Maximum number of Easy ATS (Greenhouse, Lever, etc.) jobs to scrape |\n| `--scrape-only` | `flag` | `False` | Scrapes and saves to Excel without automatically launching `run_tailor.py` |"
    modified_response: "Here are the exact answers to your two questions:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Where to See & Update the Workday and Easy Apply Counts\n\nIn your codebase and app interface, the counts are defined using the formula:\n$$\\text{Total Count} = \\text{Workday} + \\text{Easy Apply}$$\n\n#### A. In the Code (`src/data/candidateProfiles.ts`)\nYou can view and update the counts at the very top of `src/data/candidateProfiles.ts`:\n\n```typescript\n// ============================================================================\n// MAIN CONFIGURATION: WORKDAY, EASY APPLY & GLOBAL JOB FETCH LIMITS\n// ============================================================================\nexport const DEFAULT_MAX_WORKDAY_JOBS = 10;\nexport const DEFAULT_MAX_EASY_ATS_JOBS = 65;\nexport const JOBS_TO_FETCH = DEFAULT_MAX_WORKDAY_JOBS + DEFAULT_MAX_EASY_ATS_JOBS; // 75\n\n// Candidate Quotas:\n// 1. Lohith S:     Workday = 10, Easy Apply = 65, Total Count = 75\n// 2. Smit Patel:   Workday = 10, Easy Apply = 65, Total Count = 75\n// 3. Vamsi Krishna: Workday = 10, Easy Apply = 65, Total Count = 75\nexport const CANDIDATE_JOB_LIMITS = {\n  \'Lohith S\':     { workday: 10, easyAts: 65, total: 75 },\n  \'Smit Patel\':   { workday: 10, easyAts: 65, total: 75 },\n  \'Vamsi Krishna\': { workday: 10, easyAts: 65, total: 75 },\n};\n```\n\nAnd in each candidate object within the `CANDIDATES` array:\n* **LOHITH S**: `maxWorkdayJobs: 10`, `maxEasyAtsJobs: 65`, `maxTotalJobs: 75`\n* **Smit Patel**: `maxWorkdayJobs: 10`, `maxEasyAtsJobs: 65`, `maxTotalJobs: 75`\n* **Vamsi Krishna**: `maxWorkdayJobs: 10`, `maxEasyAtsJobs: 65`, `maxTotalJobs: 75`\n\n#### B. In the Live App Interface\n* Navigate to the **Multi-Candidate Automation** tab.\n* On each candidate card, you will see a dedicated quota breakdown box:\n  * **Total Count:** `75 jobs` (or your custom `JOBS_TO_FETCH`)\n  * **\342\200\242 Workday:** `10`\n  * **\342\200\242 Easy Apply:** `65`\n* The jobs table displays a **Platform (ATS)** column tagging each collected position with an amber `WORKDAY` or emerald `EASY_ATS` badge.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Run the Python Script (CLI Commands)\n\nYour Python script uses `argparse` with specific command-line flags. Here is how you run it:\n\n#### Basic Execution (Candidate Name Required)\nTo run for a specific candidate using their default config in `profiles.json`:\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\"\n```\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\"\n```\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\n#### Custom Quotas (Override Workday and Easy Apply from Command Line)\nIf you want to override the numbers dynamically when launching:\n```bash\n# Example: 15 Workday jobs + 50 Easy Apply jobs (Total = 65)\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" --workday 15 --easy 50\n```\n\n#### Scrape Only Mode (Without starting the resume customizer immediately)\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\" --scrape-only\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Available CLI Arguments:\n| Argument | Type | Default | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `--candidate` | `string` | **Required** | Candidate key in `profiles.json` (e.g. `\"Lohith S\"`, `\"Smit Patel\"`, `\"Vamsi Krishna\"`) |\n| `--workday` | `int` | `10` | Maximum number of Workday jobs to scrape |\n| `--easy` | `int` | `65` | Maximum number of Easy ATS (Greenhouse, Lever, etc.) jobs to scrape |\n| `--scrape-only` | `flag` | `False` | Scrapes and saves to Excel without automatically launching `run_tailor.py` |"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
