  planner_response {
    response: "Here is the solution to both of your requirements:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Blocked Companies (Filtered & Removed)\n\nThe blacklist has been strictly enforced across the pipeline. Any company matching any item in this list is **instantly skipped and never scraped, searched, or processed**:\n\n```python\nBLOCKED_COMPANIES = [\n    \"pinnacle\", \"google\", \"dice\", \"tcs\", \"tata consultancy\", \"ladder\", \"jobright\",\n    \"netrolynx\", \"jack & jill\", \"jack and jill\", \"chatgpt\", \"openai\", \"microsoft\",\n    \"fetchojobs\", \"fetch\", \"sundayy\", \"accenture\", \"deloitte\", \"dataannotation\",\n    \"haystack\", \"hackajob\", \"accenture federal services\"\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Single One-Line Command to Run All 3 Candidates (Scrape $\\rightarrow$ Tailor $\\rightarrow$ Compile)\n\nYou can run all three candidate scrapers sequentially or in parallel, with automatic resume generation triggered immediately after scraping.\n\n#### **Option A: Sequential One-Liner (Recommended & Cleanest)**\nRuns each candidate scraper one by one; each candidate scrapes their jobs and automatically triggers their resume generation:\n\n**On Windows (PowerShell / Terminal / CMD):**\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\n**On Linux / Mac / Bash:**\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **Option B: Master Python Runner Script (Single Clean Command)**\nIf you want to type just one short command like `python run_all.py`, create a small `run_all.py` script:\n\n```python\n# run_all.py\nimport asyncio\nimport subprocess\n\nCANDIDATES = [\"Lohith S\", \"Smit Patel\", \"Vamsi Krishna\"]\n\ndef run():\n    for candidate in CANDIDATES:\n        print(f\"\\n=======================================================\")\n        print(f\"\360\237\232\200 Starting Pipeline for candidate: {candidate}\")\n        print(f\"=======================================================\")\n        # Runs scraper and immediately triggers resume generator\n        subprocess.run([\"python\", \"scraper.py\", \"--candidate\", candidate], check=True)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run()\n```\n\nThen you can trigger all three candidates with:\n```bash\npython run_all.py\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **Option C: One-Click in the Web App Interface**\nIf using the web interface:\n1. Navigate to the **Multi-Candidate Automation** tab.\n2. Click **\"Run Full 3-Candidate Pipeline\"** in the top right.\n3. It will automatically search the jobs for all 3 candidates (enforcing the Workday & Easy Apply quotas and skipping all blacklisted companies), tailor all resumes according to their respective master LaTeX templates, and upload them to their daily Google Drive folders."
    modified_response: "Here is the solution to both of your requirements:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Blocked Companies (Filtered & Removed)\n\nThe blacklist has been strictly enforced across the pipeline. Any company matching any item in this list is **instantly skipped and never scraped, searched, or processed**:\n\n```python\nBLOCKED_COMPANIES = [\n    \"pinnacle\", \"google\", \"dice\", \"tcs\", \"tata consultancy\", \"ladder\", \"jobright\",\n    \"netrolynx\", \"jack & jill\", \"jack and jill\", \"chatgpt\", \"openai\", \"microsoft\",\n    \"fetchojobs\", \"fetch\", \"sundayy\", \"accenture\", \"deloitte\", \"dataannotation\",\n    \"haystack\", \"hackajob\", \"accenture federal services\"\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Single One-Line Command to Run All 3 Candidates (Scrape $\\rightarrow$ Tailor $\\rightarrow$ Compile)\n\nYou can run all three candidate scrapers sequentially or in parallel, with automatic resume generation triggered immediately after scraping.\n\n#### **Option A: Sequential One-Liner (Recommended & Cleanest)**\nRuns each candidate scraper one by one; each candidate scrapes their jobs and automatically triggers their resume generation:\n\n**On Windows (PowerShell / Terminal / CMD):**\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\n**On Linux / Mac / Bash:**\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **Option B: Master Python Runner Script (Single Clean Command)**\nIf you want to type just one short command like `python run_all.py`, create a small `run_all.py` script:\n\n```python\n# run_all.py\nimport asyncio\nimport subprocess\n\nCANDIDATES = [\"Lohith S\", \"Smit Patel\", \"Vamsi Krishna\"]\n\ndef run():\n    for candidate in CANDIDATES:\n        print(f\"\\n=======================================================\")\n        print(f\"\360\237\232\200 Starting Pipeline for candidate: {candidate}\")\n        print(f\"=======================================================\")\n        # Runs scraper and immediately triggers resume generator\n        subprocess.run([\"python\", \"scraper.py\", \"--candidate\", candidate], check=True)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run()\n```\n\nThen you can trigger all three candidates with:\n```bash\npython run_all.py\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **Option C: One-Click in the Web App Interface**\nIf using the web interface:\n1. Navigate to the **Multi-Candidate Automation** tab.\n2. Click **\"Run Full 3-Candidate Pipeline\"** in the top right.\n3. It will automatically search the jobs for all 3 candidates (enforcing the Workday & Easy Apply quotas and skipping all blacklisted companies), tailor all resumes according to their respective master LaTeX templates, and upload them to their daily Google Drive folders."
