  planner_response {
    response: "Here is what is happening and how to see the results clearly:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Why Did It Stop After 1\342\200\2232 Seconds?\n\nThere are two distinct tabs in the app:\n1. **The Header \"Run Pipeline\" Button** (for the classic single-sheet runner):\n   - By default, if the app is in **Live Google Workspace Mode** without an active Google Sign-in or selected rows, it logs an error/notice and halts immediately to avoid modifying unauthenticated sheets.\n2. **The \"Multi-Candidate Automation Hub\" Tab** (Your 3 Candidates: *Lohith S*, *Smit Patel*, *Vamsi Krishna*):\n   - If the jobs table for that candidate has not had jobs fetched yet (0 in queue), clicking \"Run All Jobs\" completes in 0.1 seconds because there are no jobs to process.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Know It\'s Working & How to Run It Properly\n\n#### In the Web Application:\nFollow these 3 quick steps in the preview:\n\n1. **Go to the \"Multi-Candidate Automation\" tab** (active by default).\n2. **Click \"Fetch Next 75 Jobs\"** (or use the candidate button):\n   - You will see the table populate with **75 jobs** (10 Workday, 65 Easy Apply, skipping all blocked companies like Pinnacle, Google, TCS, Dice, etc.).\n3. **Click \"Run All 75 Jobs\"** (or click **\"Generate Resume\"** on any individual job row):\n   - You will see real-time progress: `Processing (1/75)...`\n   - The status badge on the right will flip from **`PENDING` $\\rightarrow$ `SUCCESS`** (in green).\n   - A clickable **\"View Resume (Drive)\"** link and a **\"Preview PDF\"** modal button will appear immediately for each processed job.\n   - The live terminal console below will output live logs for every generated LaTeX file and Drive folder.\n\n---\n\n#### In Python (Local Terminal / Scripts):\nWhen you run the terminal command:\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\nYou can confirm it is working by checking:\n1. **Terminal Output**: It prints real-time logs:\n   - `[Search] Found job #1: Amazon - Software Engineer (ATS: WORKDAY)`\n   - `[Gemini] Tailoring LaTeX resume strictly enforcing 4 bullets per company...`\n   - `[Compilation] Generated Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf`\n   - `[Drive] Uploaded to Google Drive / Lohith S / 08-23-2026 / Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf`\n2. **Your Output Folders**:\n   - Check your output folder `output/Lohith S/` (or your Excel sheet `Lohith_S_Jobs.xlsx`) where the compiled `.pdf` files and the spreadsheet hyperlinks are written."
    modified_response: "Here is what is happening and how to see the results clearly:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Why Did It Stop After 1\342\200\2232 Seconds?\n\nThere are two distinct tabs in the app:\n1. **The Header \"Run Pipeline\" Button** (for the classic single-sheet runner):\n   - By default, if the app is in **Live Google Workspace Mode** without an active Google Sign-in or selected rows, it logs an error/notice and halts immediately to avoid modifying unauthenticated sheets.\n2. **The \"Multi-Candidate Automation Hub\" Tab** (Your 3 Candidates: *Lohith S*, *Smit Patel*, *Vamsi Krishna*):\n   - If the jobs table for that candidate has not had jobs fetched yet (0 in queue), clicking \"Run All Jobs\" completes in 0.1 seconds because there are no jobs to process.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Know It\'s Working & How to Run It Properly\n\n#### In the Web Application:\nFollow these 3 quick steps in the preview:\n\n1. **Go to the \"Multi-Candidate Automation\" tab** (active by default).\n2. **Click \"Fetch Next 75 Jobs\"** (or use the candidate button):\n   - You will see the table populate with **75 jobs** (10 Workday, 65 Easy Apply, skipping all blocked companies like Pinnacle, Google, TCS, Dice, etc.).\n3. **Click \"Run All 75 Jobs\"** (or click **\"Generate Resume\"** on any individual job row):\n   - You will see real-time progress: `Processing (1/75)...`\n   - The status badge on the right will flip from **`PENDING` $\\rightarrow$ `SUCCESS`** (in green).\n   - A clickable **\"View Resume (Drive)\"** link and a **\"Preview PDF\"** modal button will appear immediately for each processed job.\n   - The live terminal console below will output live logs for every generated LaTeX file and Drive folder.\n\n---\n\n#### In Python (Local Terminal / Scripts):\nWhen you run the terminal command:\n```bash\npython scraper.py --candidate \"Lohith S\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Smit Patel\" && python scraper.py --candidate \"Vamsi Krishna\"\n```\n\nYou can confirm it is working by checking:\n1. **Terminal Output**: It prints real-time logs:\n   - `[Search] Found job #1: Amazon - Software Engineer (ATS: WORKDAY)`\n   - `[Gemini] Tailoring LaTeX resume strictly enforcing 4 bullets per company...`\n   - `[Compilation] Generated Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf`\n   - `[Drive] Uploaded to Google Drive / Lohith S / 08-23-2026 / Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf`\n2. **Your Output Folders**:\n   - Check your output folder `output/Lohith S/` (or your Excel sheet `Lohith_S_Jobs.xlsx`) where the compiled `.pdf` files and the spreadsheet hyperlinks are written."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
