  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Job Search Flaw**\n\nI\'m digging into `searchJobsForCandidate` within `src/services/jobSearchService.ts`. The primary focus is why the function isn\'t returning the expected 75 jobs (10 Workday, 65 Easy Apply). I\'m looking for clues in the `jobSearchService` file.\n\n\n**Analyzing Search Logic Cycles**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a critical issue: the cyclical nature of the search logic in `searchJobsForCandidate`. The use of modulo operations with `TECH_COMPANIES` (25 items) and `targetRoles` (9 items) creates repetitive (company, role) pairings very quickly. When `isDuplicateJob` flags a pairing as a duplicate, the loop discards the attempt. After the loop exits, there are not enough jobs. This explains the underperforming job count; the search exhausts possible combinations prematurely because it\'s caught in a loop.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 494996523
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
