  planner_response {
    response: "### Why the Job Counts Were Showing 36, 72, and 32\n\n1. **Company Pool & Duplicate Discarding**:\n   - The company list was previously limited to ~25 companies. \n   - When filtering against candidate target roles (Lohith had 9 roles, Smit had 42 roles, Vamsi had 9 roles), the deduplication check was discarding repeated combinations. Once all unique permutations for that candidate\'s roles were exhausted, the search loop timed out and stopped early.\n   - Because Smit had 42 target roles listed, he reached 72 jobs, whereas Lohith and Vamsi had fewer roles and reached only 36 and 32 jobs.\n\n2. **Workday vs. Easy Apply Quota Alignment**:\n   - The platform had not explicitly partitioned the quota generation into exact buckets (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply).\n\n---\n\n### What Has Been Fixed\n\n1. **Expanded Enterprise Company Engine (150+ Companies)**:\n   - Added a massive verified catalog of Fortune 500 & tech companies divided across **Workday Portals** (Salesforce, Target, Walmart Tech, JPMorgan Chase, Goldman Sachs, Capital One, Visa, Mastercard, Boeing, Pfizer, etc.) and **Easy ATS Platforms** (Greenhouse, Lever, SmartRecruiters: Amazon, Apple, Meta, Netflix, Stripe, Databricks, Snowflake, Uber, Airbnb, Spotify, etc.).\n   - All 21 blacklisted companies (*Pinnacle, Google, Dice, TCS, Accenture, Deloitte, etc.*) remain strictly blocked and skipped.\n\n2. **Guaranteed Exact 75-Job Allocation for All 3 Candidates**:\n   - **Lohith S**: **75 jobs** (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply)\n   - **Smit Patel**: **75 jobs** (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply)\n   - **Vamsi Krishna**: **75 jobs** (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply)\n\n3. **Immediate Full Initial State**:\n   - When opening the app, each candidate card and table now loads with **exactly 75 unique jobs** ready to be processed."
    modified_response: "### Why the Job Counts Were Showing 36, 72, and 32\n\n1. **Company Pool & Duplicate Discarding**:\n   - The company list was previously limited to ~25 companies. \n   - When filtering against candidate target roles (Lohith had 9 roles, Smit had 42 roles, Vamsi had 9 roles), the deduplication check was discarding repeated combinations. Once all unique permutations for that candidate\'s roles were exhausted, the search loop timed out and stopped early.\n   - Because Smit had 42 target roles listed, he reached 72 jobs, whereas Lohith and Vamsi had fewer roles and reached only 36 and 32 jobs.\n\n2. **Workday vs. Easy Apply Quota Alignment**:\n   - The platform had not explicitly partitioned the quota generation into exact buckets (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply).\n\n---\n\n### What Has Been Fixed\n\n1. **Expanded Enterprise Company Engine (150+ Companies)**:\n   - Added a massive verified catalog of Fortune 500 & tech companies divided across **Workday Portals** (Salesforce, Target, Walmart Tech, JPMorgan Chase, Goldman Sachs, Capital One, Visa, Mastercard, Boeing, Pfizer, etc.) and **Easy ATS Platforms** (Greenhouse, Lever, SmartRecruiters: Amazon, Apple, Meta, Netflix, Stripe, Databricks, Snowflake, Uber, Airbnb, Spotify, etc.).\n   - All 21 blacklisted companies (*Pinnacle, Google, Dice, TCS, Accenture, Deloitte, etc.*) remain strictly blocked and skipped.\n\n2. **Guaranteed Exact 75-Job Allocation for All 3 Candidates**:\n   - **Lohith S**: **75 jobs** (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply)\n   - **Smit Patel**: **75 jobs** (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply)\n   - **Vamsi Krishna**: **75 jobs** (10 Workday + 65 Easy Apply)\n\n3. **Immediate Full Initial State**:\n   - When opening the app, each candidate card and table now loads with **exactly 75 unique jobs** ready to be processed."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
