    started_at {
      seconds: 1787536268
      nanos: 692565690
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    response: "Here is a step-by-step guide on how the entire system works, how to generate your resumes, and how to verify they are saved to Google Drive and Google Sheets.\n\n---\n\n### 1. How the Pipeline Works (Behind the Scenes)\n\nFor each candidate (**Lohith S**, **Smit Patel**, or **Vamsi Krishna**), the system runs an automated 4-stage engine:\n\n1. **Job Sourcing (75 Jobs Queue)**:\n   - Allocates **10 Workday Enterprise** jobs + **65 Easy Apply ATS** jobs (Greenhouse, Lever, SmartRecruiters).\n   - Skips all 21 blacklisted recruitment agencies and platforms (*Pinnacle, Google, Dice, TCS, Wipro, etc.*).\n2. **Gemini 3.7 Flash LaTeX Customization**:\n   - Takes the job description and the candidate\'s verified Master Profile.\n   - Adjusts skills, summary, and bullet points while strictly enforcing the template rules (e.g. **exact 4 bullets per role**, 5+ years experience formatting).\n3. **PDF Compilation**:\n   - Compiles the LaTeX document into a named PDF: `<Candidate Name> 5EXP <Index>.pdf` (e.g., `Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf`).\n4. **Google Workspace Sync (Drive & Sheets)**:\n   - Uploads the PDF to Google Drive in the candidate\'s daily folder (e.g., `/Lohith S/08-23-2026/`).\n   - Appends a new row to the candidate\'s Google Sheet with the date, company, job title, ATS portal, and a clickable link to the PDF in Drive.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Generate Resumes (Step-by-Step)\n\n#### Step 1: Open the App in a Full Browser Tab (Crucial for Google Sign-in)\nBecause Google blocks sign-in popups inside small embedded iframes, open the app directly:\n\360\237\221\211 **[Open App in Full Tab](https://ais-dev-zpb346tbd45k7imxcrlrmz-883765664887.asia-southeast1.run.app)**\n\n#### Step 2: Connect Your Google Account\n* In the top navigation bar, click the **\"Connect Google Account\"** or **\"Sign In with Google\"** button.\n* Authorize access so the app has permission to create folders in your Google Drive and add rows to your Google Sheets.\n\n#### Step 3: Select Your Candidate\n* At the top of the **Multi-Candidate Hub**, select one of the three candidates:\n  * \360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\222\273 **Lohith S** (Software Engineer \342\200\224 Java / Spring / Python / AWS)\n  * \360\237\223\212 **Smit Patel** (Business / Data Analyst \342\200\224 SQL / Tableau / Power BI / Agile)\n  * \360\237\214\220 **Vamsi Krishna** (Full Stack Developer \342\200\224 React / TypeScript / Node / Cloud)\n\n#### Step 4: Run Resume Generation\nYou can run jobs in two ways:\n* **Option A: Run All 75 at once**:\n  Click the blue **\"Run All 75 Jobs\"** button in the queue header. The app will process each job sequentially.\n* **Option B: Generate one by one**:\n  Click the **\"Generate Resume\"** button on any individual job row in the table.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How to Know They Are Saved in Drive and Google Sheets\n\nAs soon as a job finishes processing, you will see immediate visual proof in three places:\n\n#### 1. In the Web App Table\n* The job\'s status badge turns from gray `PENDING` to green **`SUCCESS`**.\n* A blue **`PDF`** button appears \342\200\224 click it to preview the generated resume directly in your browser.\n* A green **`Drive Link`** button appears \342\200\224 click it to open that specific PDF in your Google Drive.\n\n#### 2. Direct Folder & Sheet Buttons\nOn the candidate card at the top, click:\n* \360\237\223\201 **`Drive Folder`** (amber button): Opens the candidate\'s folder in your Google Drive where all daily `.pdf` files are stored.\n* \360\237\223\212 **`Google Sheet`** (emerald button): Opens the spreadsheet where each row logs the job details and the direct PDF hyperlink.\n\n#### 3. Live Execution Terminal (at bottom of screen)\nThe terminal will display live log messages confirming each step:\n```text\n[GEMINI] Generating tailored LaTeX for Amazon - Software Engineer...\n[COMPILER] Output compiled: Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf\n[DRIVE] Uploaded to /Lohith S/08-23-2026/Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf\n[SHEETS] Appended row to Lohith S tab in Tracking Sheet.\n```"
    modified_response: "Here is a step-by-step guide on how the entire system works, how to generate your resumes, and how to verify they are saved to Google Drive and Google Sheets.\n\n---\n\n### 1. How the Pipeline Works (Behind the Scenes)\n\nFor each candidate (**Lohith S**, **Smit Patel**, or **Vamsi Krishna**), the system runs an automated 4-stage engine:\n\n1. **Job Sourcing (75 Jobs Queue)**:\n   - Allocates **10 Workday Enterprise** jobs + **65 Easy Apply ATS** jobs (Greenhouse, Lever, SmartRecruiters).\n   - Skips all 21 blacklisted recruitment agencies and platforms (*Pinnacle, Google, Dice, TCS, Wipro, etc.*).\n2. **Gemini 3.7 Flash LaTeX Customization**:\n   - Takes the job description and the candidate\'s verified Master Profile.\n   - Adjusts skills, summary, and bullet points while strictly enforcing the template rules (e.g. **exact 4 bullets per role**, 5+ years experience formatting).\n3. **PDF Compilation**:\n   - Compiles the LaTeX document into a named PDF: `<Candidate Name> 5EXP <Index>.pdf` (e.g., `Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf`).\n4. **Google Workspace Sync (Drive & Sheets)**:\n   - Uploads the PDF to Google Drive in the candidate\'s daily folder (e.g., `/Lohith S/08-23-2026/`).\n   - Appends a new row to the candidate\'s Google Sheet with the date, company, job title, ATS portal, and a clickable link to the PDF in Drive.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Generate Resumes (Step-by-Step)\n\n#### Step 1: Open the App in a Full Browser Tab (Crucial for Google Sign-in)\nBecause Google blocks sign-in popups inside small embedded iframes, open the app directly:\n\360\237\221\211 **[Open App in Full Tab](https://ais-dev-zpb346tbd45k7imxcrlrmz-883765664887.asia-southeast1.run.app)**\n\n#### Step 2: Connect Your Google Account\n* In the top navigation bar, click the **\"Connect Google Account\"** or **\"Sign In with Google\"** button.\n* Authorize access so the app has permission to create folders in your Google Drive and add rows to your Google Sheets.\n\n#### Step 3: Select Your Candidate\n* At the top of the **Multi-Candidate Hub**, select one of the three candidates:\n  * \360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\222\273 **Lohith S** (Software Engineer \342\200\224 Java / Spring / Python / AWS)\n  * \360\237\223\212 **Smit Patel** (Business / Data Analyst \342\200\224 SQL / Tableau / Power BI / Agile)\n  * \360\237\214\220 **Vamsi Krishna** (Full Stack Developer \342\200\224 React / TypeScript / Node / Cloud)\n\n#### Step 4: Run Resume Generation\nYou can run jobs in two ways:\n* **Option A: Run All 75 at once**:\n  Click the blue **\"Run All 75 Jobs\"** button in the queue header. The app will process each job sequentially.\n* **Option B: Generate one by one**:\n  Click the **\"Generate Resume\"** button on any individual job row in the table.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How to Know They Are Saved in Drive and Google Sheets\n\nAs soon as a job finishes processing, you will see immediate visual proof in three places:\n\n#### 1. In the Web App Table\n* The job\'s status badge turns from gray `PENDING` to green **`SUCCESS`**.\n* A blue **`PDF`** button appears \342\200\224 click it to preview the generated resume directly in your browser.\n* A green **`Drive Link`** button appears \342\200\224 click it to open that specific PDF in your Google Drive.\n\n#### 2. Direct Folder & Sheet Buttons\nOn the candidate card at the top, click:\n* \360\237\223\201 **`Drive Folder`** (amber button): Opens the candidate\'s folder in your Google Drive where all daily `.pdf` files are stored.\n* \360\237\223\212 **`Google Sheet`** (emerald button): Opens the spreadsheet where each row logs the job details and the direct PDF hyperlink.\n\n#### 3. Live Execution Terminal (at bottom of screen)\nThe terminal will display live log messages confirming each step:\n```text\n[GEMINI] Generating tailored LaTeX for Amazon - Software Engineer...\n[COMPILER] Output compiled: Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf\n[DRIVE] Uploaded to /Lohith S/08-23-2026/Lohith S 5EXP 1.pdf\n[SHEETS] Appended row to Lohith S tab in Tracking Sheet.\n```"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
