    response: "Based on the screenshots you provided, the application has been updated to match your exact Google Drive folder structures, PDF file naming conventions, and Google Spreadsheet dashboard formats.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Google Drive Structure (Matching Screenshot 1)\n\nAll files and folders now follow the format seen in your Drive screenshot:\n\n- **Drive Folder Name**: `<Candidate><Day>-<Month>` (e.g., `Vamsi24-8`, `Lohith24-8`, `Smit24-8`)\n- **Drive Folder Link**: Configured directly to your exact folder:  \n  \360\237\221\211 `https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1C9K9g8ImqLndPcNxKAhR6nHq4E8W2NOY`\n- **Resume File Names**: `<FirstName>_Resume<Exp>exp<Count>.pdf`\n  - `Vamsi_Resume5exp1.pdf`\n  - `Vamsi_Resume5exp2.pdf`\n  - `Vamsi_Resume5exp3.pdf`\n  - ... up to your quota count.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Google Spreadsheet Structure (Matching Screenshot 2)\n\n- **Spreadsheet Title**: `Vamsi Krishna (Dev) Dashboard` (with tabs `Vamsi24-8`, `Lohith24-8`, `Smit24-8`)\n- **Required Columns Formatted in Order**:\n  1. **Company**\n  2. **Role**\n  3. **Location**\n  4. **Job URL**\n  5. **Resume File Name** (`Vamsi_Resume5exp1.pdf`)\n  6. **Google Drive Folder** (`Vamsi24-8`)\n  7. **Drive PDF Link**\n  8. **Candidate**\n  9. **Status**\n\n---\n\n### 3. Share Your Drive & Spreadsheet URLs\n\nYou can provide your specific spreadsheet and folder URLs by pasting them in your next message. For example:\n- **Lohith S**: Drive Folder URL & Google Sheet URL\n- **Smit Patel**: Drive Folder URL & Google Sheet URL\n- **Vamsi Krishna**: Already pre-configured with folder ID `1C9K9g8ImqLndPcNxKAhR6nHq4E8W2NOY`\n\n---\n\n### 4. Running the Complete Automation\n\n1. Open the updated dashboard:  \n   \360\237\221\211 **[https://ais-dev-zpb346tbd45k7imxcrlrmz-883765664887.asia-southeast1.run.app](https://ais-dev-zpb346tbd45k7imxcrlrmz-883765664887.asia-southeast1.run.app)**\n2. Click **`\342\232\241 Complete All 3 Candidates (320 Resumes)`**.\n3. In the popup modal, click **`Copy All for Google Sheets`** and paste (`Cmd+V` / `Ctrl+V`) directly into your `Vamsi Krishna (Dev) Dashboard` spreadsheet."
    modified_response: "Based on the screenshots you provided, the application has been updated to match your exact Google Drive folder structures, PDF file naming conventions, and Google Spreadsheet dashboard formats.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Google Drive Structure (Matching Screenshot 1)\n\nAll files and folders now follow the format seen in your Drive screenshot:\n\n- **Drive Folder Name**: `<Candidate><Day>-<Month>` (e.g., `Vamsi24-8`, `Lohith24-8`, `Smit24-8`)\n- **Drive Folder Link**: Configured directly to your exact folder:  \n  \360\237\221\211 `https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1C9K9g8ImqLndPcNxKAhR6nHq4E8W2NOY`\n- **Resume File Names**: `<FirstName>_Resume<Exp>exp<Count>.pdf`\n  - `Vamsi_Resume5exp1.pdf`\n  - `Vamsi_Resume5exp2.pdf`\n  - `Vamsi_Resume5exp3.pdf`\n  - ... up to your quota count.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Google Spreadsheet Structure (Matching Screenshot 2)\n\n- **Spreadsheet Title**: `Vamsi Krishna (Dev) Dashboard` (with tabs `Vamsi24-8`, `Lohith24-8`, `Smit24-8`)\n- **Required Columns Formatted in Order**:\n  1. **Company**\n  2. **Role**\n  3. **Location**\n  4. **Job URL**\n  5. **Resume File Name** (`Vamsi_Resume5exp1.pdf`)\n  6. **Google Drive Folder** (`Vamsi24-8`)\n  7. **Drive PDF Link**\n  8. **Candidate**\n  9. **Status**\n\n---\n\n### 3. Share Your Drive & Spreadsheet URLs\n\nYou can provide your specific spreadsheet and folder URLs by pasting them in your next message. For example:\n- **Lohith S**: Drive Folder URL & Google Sheet URL\n- **Smit Patel**: Drive Folder URL & Google Sheet URL\n- **Vamsi Krishna**: Already pre-configured with folder ID `1C9K9g8ImqLndPcNxKAhR6nHq4E8W2NOY`\n\n---\n\n### 4. Running the Complete Automation\n\n1. Open the updated dashboard:  \n   \360\237\221\211 **[https://ais-dev-zpb346tbd45k7imxcrlrmz-883765664887.asia-southeast1.run.app](https://ais-dev-zpb346tbd45k7imxcrlrmz-883765664887.asia-southeast1.run.app)**\n2. Click **`\342\232\241 Complete All 3 Candidates (320 Resumes)`**.\n3. In the popup modal, click 